                <pb facs="1008" n="892" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg892"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.00/2672a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in the
                        Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-02-14T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 14,
                                1923—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>6. The Department desires to be kept promptly and fully informed regarding
                    political conditions in Santo Domingo. Department has not yet been informed of
                    promulgation of electoral law, or if it has not yet been promulgated, as to the
                    reasons for its delay. Please report in detail regarding this and all other
                    political matters.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
